SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F327A1786722499
OL,3,CHow and when to watch the solar
OL,4,Ceclipse in Cumbria and southern
OL,5,CScotland
OL,7,FSource: timeanddate.com info
OL,9,FThe eclipse begins and peaks earlier
OL,10,Fthe further north you are, while those
OL,11,Ffurther west will experience more
OL,12,Fcoverage at its maximum.
OL,14,FIn Dumfries, the peak will happen at
OL,15,F7:07pm, Galashiels will see its peak
OL,16,Fat 7:06pm, while in Kendal the peak
OL,17,Feclipse will be seen at 7.08pm.
OL,19,FThose in Kendal will witness 91.22%
OL,20,Fcoverage, while people in Coldstream
OL,21,Fwill witness 90.29% coverage.
OL,1,W{$~k4{$k4~sjw=                 G4/6
