OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F327A1786722499
OL,3,CHow and when to watch the solar
OL,4,Ceclipse in Cumbria and southern
OL,5,CScotland
OL,7,FITV Border's weather presenter Ross
OL,8,FHutchinson explains what the
OL,9,Fconditions will be like for eclipse
OL,10,Fviewing in our region
OL,12,FHow do I watch it?
OL,14,FThe partial eclipse will be low in the
OL,15,Fhorizon - making it appear bigger.
OL,17,FThis means you have to have a view of
OL,18,Fthe western horizon, and ideally not
OL,19,Fbe surrounded by buildings or trees.
OL,1,W{$~k4{$k4~sjw=                 G5/6
